    <summary>Toolbox for easy launching the official Valve SDKs such as Source SDK 2013 SP or MP.</summary>
    <description>Universal Valve Toolbox is a launcher for the official Valve SDKs and the tools of Source engine games: pick a game you own on Steam (Source SDK 2013 Singleplayer / Multiplayer, Half-Life 2, Portal, Team Fortress 2, Left 4 Dead 2, Garry's Mod, Black Mesa, Source Filmmaker and more - see the [list of supported games](https://github.com/EpicMorg/UniversalValveToolbox/blob/master/SUPPORTED.md)) and start Hammer, Model Viewer, Faceposer and the other SDK tools, your mod projects and helper apps from one window.

`Universal Valve Toolbox is not affiliated with Valve Corporation.`

## Features
- Detects the installed Source games and SDKs through Steam
- Engine, tool and addon definitions are JSON files (`json\engines`, `json\addons`) - easy to extend
- Projects (mods) with their own launch options
- Modes `retail` (default), `bundle` (ship it with your game) and `dev` - see [SETTINGS.md](https://github.com/EpicMorg/UniversalValveToolbox/blob/master/SETTINGS.md)
- English, Russian and Ukrainian UI

## Package notes
- Portable: the official release zip is extracted into the package folder; `UniversalValveToolbox` (GUI shim) is put on the PATH and a Start menu shortcut is created.
- Needs .NET Framework 4.8 (dependency) and a running Steam client.
- The toolbox keeps `settings.json` and your projects in its own `json` folder: the package lets users write there and keeps `json\settings.json` and `json\projects` over upgrades (a copy is kept in `%ProgramData%\EpicMorg\UniversalValveToolbox`).
</description>
    <releaseNotes>## 1.0.0.0 - 2020-03-19

- Release Candidate (published as a pre-release).

Release: https://github.com/EpicMorg/UniversalValveToolbox/releases/tag/1.0.0.0
</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
